libstdc++ 13's <format>: the four inline std::vformat overloads
(format:3784/3793/3802/3811) are dropped with "scope '__format' is
ambiguous" -- the class template __format::_Arg_store is declared in
namespace std::__format, defined outside it by a qualified name, and the
namespace is reopened afterwards; see test.desc (header-free, from the
cvise reduction in /tmp/r163/red/kb_K).  Calling std::vformat from user
code additionally fails in basic_format_args<nil> ("symbol '_CharT' is
unknown"), to be split out when this is fixed.  Round-163 audit:
cpp20_format_header.  Pre-existing (round-162 snapshot bin51).
